From b54c72b4c2c9e989b81693525ee5a4bb5b0fcfdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:44:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add TR-069 (CWMP) settings page under System

New System > TR-069 page to configure the vendor cwmpClient: ACS URL /
username / password, periodic inform + interval, connection request
username / password / path / port, the TR-069 daemon (AUTORUN) switch and
the EnableCWMP switch, plus a live Running/Stopped badge and a manual
"Restart TR-069 client" button.

Backend mirrors the vendor firmware's own TR-069 page (SDK: boa
form_src_generic/fmtr069.c, utility.c off_tr069/startCWMP/restart_cwmp_acl):
- tr069.cgi: status/save/restart. Validates all input server-side before
  touching the MIB, only writes values that changed, rolls back on a failed
  `mib set` or `mib commit`, and updates CWMP_FLAG / CWMP_FLAG2
  read-modify-write on just the bits it owns (AUTORUN 0x20, CWMP_DISABLE
  0x80) since those bytes also carry unrelated state bits. Records the
  previous ACS URL in /var/oldacs like vendor storeOldACS().
- tr069_ctl.sh: detached restart (SIGTERM via /var/run/cwmp.pid, wait,
  start /bin/cwmpClient only if AUTORUN is set). When the connection request
  port changes and the CWMP ACL is off, rebuilds the mangle/cwmp_aclblock
  mark rule for the new port; with the ACL on it leaves the firewall alone.
- nav.js: System > TR-069 entry.

Not covered: the CWMP ACL IP table, TR-111 STUN and the ACS/CPE
certificate pages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SrzZq6FFfoQQLFDEXkhV1C
